(gen_random_uuid(), 'taylor-swift-nashville-songwriters-hall-of-fame-induction-20261027', 'taylor-swift', 'United States',
'Taylor Swift Inducted Into Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame as Its Youngest-Ever Member',
'टेलर स्विफ्ट न्यासभिल साङराइटर्स हल अफ फेममा सबैभन्दा कान्छी सदस्यका रूपमा समावेश',
'Taylor Swift was formally inducted into the Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame on 26 October 2026, becoming the institution''s youngest-ever member at the age of 36, at its 56th Anniversary Gala at the Music City Center in Nashville.',
'टेलर स्विफ्ट २६ अक्टोबर २०२६ मा न्यासभिल साङराइटर्स हल अफ फेममा औपचारिक रूपमा समावेश भइन् र ३६ वर्षको उमेरमा उक्त संस्थाकी सबैभन्दा कान्छी सदस्य बनिन्। यो सम्मान न्यासभिलको म्युजिक सिटी सेन्टरमा आयोजित ५६औँ वार्षिकोत्सव गालामा प्रदान गरिएको हो।',
$$<p>Taylor Swift was formally inducted into the Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame on the evening of 26 October 2026, becoming the institution's youngest-ever member at the age of 36. The honour was presented at the organisation's 56th Anniversary Gala at the Music City Center in Nashville, where Swift was introduced by fellow musician Brad Paisley, <a href="https://particle.news/story/taylor-swift-becomes-youngest-inductee-into-nashville-songwriters-hall-of-fame">Particle reported</a>. Page Six, which covered the gala on the night, likewise described the moment as history-making. The induction closes a year in which Swift has been recognised twice specifically as a songwriter, and it returns her to the city where her career as a writer began.</p>
<h2>At a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Event</th><td>Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame, 56th Anniversary Gala</td></tr>
<tr><th>Date and place</th><td>26 October 2026, Music City Center, Nashville</td></tr>
<tr><th>Honouree</th><td>Taylor Swift, inducted at age 36 as the youngest-ever member</td></tr>
<tr><th>Presented by</th><td>Brad Paisley</td></tr>
<tr><th>Fellow inductees</th><td>Lyle Lovett, Lee Thomas Miller, Shawn Camp, Bruce Channel, and J.I. Allison (posthumous)</td></tr>
<tr><th>Other award</th><td>George Strait received the Career Maker Award</td></tr>
<tr><th>Tribute performance</th><td>Lainey Wilson performed an acoustic version of "Love Story"</td></tr>
<tr><th>Earlier 2026 honour</th><td>Songwriters Hall of Fame, New York, June 2026 — youngest woman inducted</td></tr>
</table>
<h2>The night in Nashville</h2>
<p>Swift was one of six inductees in the Class of 2026. Alongside her, the hall inducted Lyle Lovett, Lee Thomas Miller, Shawn Camp and Bruce Channel, with the late J.I. Allison honoured posthumously, Particle reported. The same ceremony presented George Strait with the Career Maker Award. InMusic gave the same six-name class and the same Strait award, and confirmed that Paisley introduced Swift.</p>
<p>The musical tribute came from Lainey Wilson, who performed a stripped-down acoustic version of Swift's "Love Story", Particle reported. InMusic reported that Swift thanked Wilson, calling her one of the coolest people in the world and praising her single "Kinda Love It". "Love Story", released in 2008, was one of the early songs that carried Swift from Nashville country songwriting to a worldwide audience.</p>
<p>Paisley's introduction also brought a lighter moment. InMusic reported that Swift joked about a prank from their 2007 tour, when thousands of live crickets were released on her tour bus. She recalled being kept awake by the insects for months, before suggesting that Paisley's induction speech had finally made amends possible.</p>
<h2>What Swift said</h2>
<p>In her acceptance speech, Swift spoke about Nashville's influence, calling the city a middle-school daydream and saying the honour felt "crazy", Particle reported. In a statement issued at the time of her nomination, reported by Page Six, she put it more fully: "From the time I started writing songs as a child, I fixated on Nashville as the perfect place to be. I wanted to learn with and from the best and get to immerse myself in a community of storytellers, and thankfully, Nashville turned out to be exactly what I'd dreamed of."</p>
<p>The same statement continued: "A town that validated and prioritized hard work, determination and imagination. Where the writers show up to work every day even when the mysterious muses and the magic don't. To be honored by this city I love so much is a beautiful thing, and I'm very grateful." That is the language of a working songwriter, and Swift's speech on the night kept the same register.</p>
<h2>The look on the night</h2>
<p>For the gala, Swift wore a burgundy velvet Raisa Vanessa dress with a floral print, worn as a strapless mini, Page Six reported, with purple Jimmy Choo heels finished with delicate crystal ankle straps and her hair in a softly curled half-up style. Page Six described the choice as a return to her roots.</p>
<h2>Why Nashville matters in her story</h2>
<p>The induction carries particular weight because Nashville is where Swift's songwriting career began. Her family moved from Pennsylvania to Tennessee when she was a teenager so that she could pursue country music, InMusic reported. Her self-titled debut album, released on 24 October 2006, introduced her as a teenage country songwriter, and its 20th anniversary fell just two days before the gala, on 24 October 2026.</p>
<p>The Nashville honour also follows a second major songwriting recognition earlier in 2026. In June 2026, Swift was inducted into the Songwriters Hall of Fame in New York, becoming the youngest woman ever inducted into that institution and its second-youngest inductee overall, behind Stevie Wonder, InMusic reported. She had also received the Songwriter-Artist of the Decade Award from the Nashville Songwriters Association International in 2022. Together, the two 2026 inductions mark a year in which Swift has been recognised specifically as a writer.</p>
<p>That songwriting emphasis has a recent commercial echo. Page Six reported that Swift's original song for "Toy Story 5", "I Knew It, I Knew You", reached No. 1 on the US country radio chart in September 2026, becoming her first tune to top that list in 13 years. Particle likewise noted a recent country radio No. 1 for the same song.</p>
<h2>What to watch next</h2>
<p>Three open questions follow. The first is the debut re-recording: Swift has finished re-recording her self-titled debut album, and she owns the original masters after buying the master recordings of her first six studio albums from Shamrock Capital in May 2025, but she has given no release date for the new version, and the gala reports seen for this article contained no such announcement. The second is whether the country return continues: a country radio No. 1 in September 2026 and a Nashville honour in October 2026 invite attention to what Swift writes next. The third is the simplest: future inductions will be measured against a 36-year-old benchmark set on 26 October 2026.</p>
<p>For now, the fact stands on its own. On 26 October 2026, at the Music City Center in Nashville, Taylor Swift was formally inducted as the Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame's youngest-ever member, introduced by Brad Paisley, serenaded with "Love Story" by Lainey Wilson, and honoured alongside Lyle Lovett, Lee Thomas Miller, Shawn Camp, Bruce Channel and J.I. Allison, with George Strait receiving the Career Maker Award on the same night.</p>$$,
$$<p>टेलर स्विफ्ट २६ अक्टोबर २०२६ को साँझ न्यासभिल साङराइटर्स हल अफ फेममा औपचारिक रूपमा समावेश भइन् र ३६ वर्षको उमेरमा उक्त संस्थाकी सबैभन्दा कान्छी सदस्य बनिन्। यो सम्मान न्यासभिलको म्युजिक सिटी सेन्टरमा आयोजित संस्थाको ५६औँ वार्षिकोत्सव गालामा प्रदान गरियो, जहाँ उनलाई साथी सङ्गीतकार ब्राड पेजलीले परिचय गराए, <a href="https://particle.news/story/taylor-swift-becomes-youngest-inductee-into-nashville-songwriters-hall-of-fame">पार्टिकलले जनाएको छ</a>। गालाको रातमा रिपोर्टिङ गरेको पेज सिक्सले पनि यो क्षणलाई इतिहास रच्ने खालको भनेको छ। यो समावेशले गीतकारका रूपमा उनलाई दुईपटक मान्यता दिइएको वर्षलाई समापन गर्छ र औपचारिक रूपमा उनलाई आफ्नो करियर लेखकका रूपमा सुरु भएको सहरमा फर्काउँछ।</p>
